<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thabo Mbeki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thabo Mbeki is a South African politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 1999 to 2008, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>. A leading ANC diplomat in exile, he presided over steady economic growth and promoted an &quot;African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>&quot;, but his questioning of the scientific consensus on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiv-aids">HIV/AIDS</a> was widely condemned. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacob-zuma">Jacob Zuma</a> for the ANC leadership at Polokwane in 2007, he was recalled in 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thabo-mbeki.jpg" alt="Thabo Mbeki" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thabo_Mbeki,_August_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
